    "replies": [
      {
        "id": "7aa6fdf1bad558b2dfcb12b8402641a7",
        "source_id": "49508981",
        "content": {
          "text": "Same interview process. Recruiter call, Live coding, System design, Behaviour interview. The only difference is that in the Live coding session they now allow AI to be used. I didn’t use it and went old way (because I had already rehearsed it the old way, and found no feedback on the internet about how the company assess AI usage, so I didn’t want to be the Guinea pig) Interview took place this summer. Major tech company in EU (not faang tho). Also Live coding is not leetcode. reply",
          "format": "text",
          "media": []
        },
        "created_at": "2026-08-31T16:03:23.364534",
        "updated_at": "2026-08-31T16:03:23.364534",
        "author": {
          "id": "f5dde00778fdf68564c59a9c85fb4020",
          "source_id": "sdevonoes",
          "username": "sdevonoes",
          "avatar": "",
          "role": "user"
        },
        "parent_id": "",
        "quote_id": "",
        "stats": {
          "likes": 0,
          "dislikes": 0
        },
        "quoted_users": []
      },
      {
        "id": "3af96a97efbe02b131b23eb67a55b06a",
        "source_id": "49508255",
        "content": {
          "text": "Did a few interviews during the summer and received 2 offers. No AI involved, except screening the CV. But one thing is very common. It's that the cultural fit interviews are longer and carry more value than ever (possibly more than technical interview). Out of 5 stages, 2 or 3 are meeting non tech people, coming to the office, having an informal chat, etc. Companies really want to know you as a person and are very careful who they pick. It's the same for remote, hybrid or office based work. reply",
          "format": "text",
          "media": []
        },
        "created_at": "2026-08-31T16:03:23.365097",
        "updated_at": "2026-08-31T16:03:23.365097",
        "author": {
          "id": "ba8321153b6e56becf911edc33aafd0c",
          "source_id": "vertigolimbo",
          "username": "vertigolimbo",
          "avatar": "",
          "role": "user"
        },
        "parent_id": "",
        "quote_id": "",
        "stats": {
          "likes": 0,
          "dislikes": 0
        },
        "quoted_users": []
      },
      {
        "id": "8d50bd831c8781ba0b6e68471951a826",
        "source_id": "49507631",
        "content": {
          "text": "Yes, something different.\n5 stages interviews are more common now, technical questions during first HR interview (they record and use transcript), personal projects don't matter, recommendation don't matter. Thinking about which profession to choose next, cause I'm not passing so many gates so far. reply",
          "format": "text",
          "media": []
        },
